Version: 0.8.0
Command: monochange migrate audit

Report existing release tools, changelog providers, and CI migration work

[1m[97mUsage:[0m [93mmonochange migrate audit[0m [95m[OPTIONS][0m

[1m[96mOptions:[0m
      [93m--format[0m[95m [0m[95m<format>[0m
          Output format
          
          [default: text]
          [possible values: text, json, markdown, md]

  [93m-h[0m, [93m--help[0m
          Print help

[1m[96mGlobal Options:[0m
  [93m-q[0m, [93m--quiet[0m
          Suppress stdout/stderr output and run in dry-run mode when supported

      [93m--progress-format[0m[95m [0m[95m<FORMAT>[0m
          Control progress output on stderr
          
          [possible values: auto, unicode, ascii, json]

      [93m--jq[0m[95m [0m[95m<EXPRESSION>[0m
          Filter JSON output with a jq-style expression, such as `.assets[].name`

      [93m--snapshot[0m
          Print a normalized JSON snapshot for this command subtree

Examples:
  monochange migrate audit
  monochange migrate audit --format json

Audit notes:
  - Looks for known release tools such as knope, Changesets, release-please, semantic-release, and cargo-release.
  - Scans GitHub Actions workflows for legacy release actions and commands.
  - Reports changelog providers and trusted-publishing migration recommendations.
